{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791002003,"nonce":"aNAo8rOoj1pwmrTaNmkyCavKrks=","title":"caribou run aborts compiling a linked wasm program on aarch64: PCRel32 jump without a veneer","message":"On macOS aarch64, `caribou run` on a Haxe program built for wasm32-wasip1 with a plugin linked panics in Cranelift while wasmtime compiles the module:\n\n    cranelift-codegen-0.130.2/src/machinst/buffer.rs:1482:9:\n    jump beyond the range of PCRel32 but a veneer isn't supported\n\nReproducer, both failing the same way at caribou 80a10b0 plus the uncommitted fcfa07e work (the second program uses no enums):\n\n    LLVM_SYS_211_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm cargo test -p caribou-driver --features llvm --test linked a_plugin_crate_links_into_a_wasm_program\n    LLVM_SYS_211_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm cargo test -p caribou-driver --features llvm --test linked plugin_data_crosses\n\nThe modules grew from about 10.8 MB (built 2026-09-28) to about 40.8 MB. The code section is about 34 MB over 8592 functions; the largest are Ash's `ash_native_call::dispatch_8_*` tables, about 250 KB each, 143 `ash_native_call` functions in all. Ash 59a945e (\"Cover all native call signatures through eight arguments\", 2026-09-29) is in the pinned ash 555af2d and postdates the smaller build.\n\nNot yet established: whether the size alone trips the aarch64 backend (x86_64 CI passes at 80a10b0), and whether a newer wasmtime/Cranelift lays out the module without the out-of-range jump. Candidate directions: generate fewer dispatch arities into a linked wasm program (only those the program's natives use), or raise the wasmtime version.","files":null}]}